@startuml
!include ../_style.iuml
title Epic 7 — Accounts and privacy

rectangle "Accounts and privacy" {
  card US7_1 [
    **US-7.1  Create an account**
    As a //new reader//, I want to sign up with my email and a password,
    so that my notebooks are mine and nobody else's.
    ----
    * The email is unique, compared case-insensitively.
    * The password has at least AUTH_PASSWORD_MIN_LENGTH characters; it is stored as an argon2id hash.
    * Signing up signs me in.
  ]
  card US7_2 [
    **US-7.2  Sign in and out**
    As a //reader//, I want to sign in on any browser and sign out when I am done,
    so that a shared computer does not keep my notebooks open.
    ----
    * A wrong password and an unknown email give the same answer.
    * Repeated failures lock the email for AUTH_LOGIN_LOCKOUT_MINUTES.
    * "Sign out everywhere" ends every session; changing the password ends all the others.
  ]
  card US7_3 [
    **US-7.3  Nobody else sees my data**
    As a //reader//, I want every notebook, source, answer, Studio item and task to be visible only to me,
    so that I can upload private documents.
    ----
    * Every data route needs a session (401 without one).
    * Another user's id answers 404, exactly as if it did not exist.
    * A test walks every route to prove it, including routes added later.
  ]
  card US7_4 [
    **US-7.4  Keep the notebooks I already had**
    As a //reader from before accounts//, I want my first signup to take over my old profile,
    so that I do not lose my notebooks.
    ----
    * Only a profile with no credentials can be claimed, and only once.
  ]
}
US7_1 -[hidden]down- US7_2
US7_2 -[hidden]down- US7_3
US7_3 -[hidden]down- US7_4
@enduml
